<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haarlem</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haarlem is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, capital of the province of North Holland, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a>. Chartered in 1245, it was a residence of the counts of Holland and a centre of brewing, linen bleaching and cloth. It held out against a seven-month Spanish siege in 1572–1573 before surrendering, and in the Golden Age it was home to painters such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frans-hals">Frans Hals</a>. The first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> railway linked it to Amsterdam in 1839.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haarlem.jpg" alt="Haarlem" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fryslan0109 at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HaarlemGroteMarkt1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
